{"case_id":"C058","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API protocol","input semantics"],"confidence":96,"affected_functions":["wuffs_base__token__value","wuffs_base__token__value_extension","wuffs_base__token__value_major","wuffs_base__token__value_base_category","wuffs_base__token__value_minor","wuffs_base__token__value_base_detail","wuffs_base__token__length"],"reason":"H0 exercises token accessors only on tokens emitted by wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens and explicitly rejects every token whose repr high bit is set. S1 makes that high bit select a new extended-token representation, adds wuffs_base__token__value_extension, and changes several accessor return values to signed, sign-extended semantics. Consequently H0 cannot exercise the extended-token branch or arbitrary 64-bit token representations at the public token-accessor boundary.","evidence":["fuzz_one_token returns \"token high bit was not zero\" whenever (t.repr >> 63) != 0.","H0 obtains tested tokens from wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens; it does not fuzz wuffs_base__make_token with arbitrary repr values.","S1 documents bit 63 as extended (1) versus simple (0), with bits 62..18 holding the bitwise-not of value_extension for extended tokens.","S1 adds wuffs_base__token__value_extension and changes wuffs_base__token__value, wuffs_base__token__value_major, and wuffs_base__token__value_base_category from uint64_t masked extraction to int64_t arithmetic-shift behavior."],"recommended_action":"Add a token-accessor fuzz path that constructs wuffs_base__token values from arbitrary 64-bit repr inputs and validates simple and extended decoding, signed sentinel behavior, link bits, and length against an independent bit-level model, emphasizing bit-63 and shift-boundary values."}
